course: dictionary
lesson: 505
title: Serious words: assassinate
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Assassinate means to murder an important or famous person, such as a leader, usually for political reasons. You can work this out from the context: the victim is someone important, and the reason is often about power or politics, not an ordinary quarrel.
explain: The spy slang «Terminate with extreme prejudice» means the same thing: to murder an important or chosen person on purpose. The words on purpose tell you the killing was planned, not an accident.
explain: Try your meaning in a sentence. «The plotters planned to assassinate the king.» Does "planned to murder the king, usually for political reasons" fit? Yes, so your meaning works. Assassinate is a serious word about violence, so you will meet it in history lessons and in news about famous leaders.
fact: Assassinate is a verb: assassinate, assassinates, assassinated, assassinating.
fact: «Assassinate» means to murder an important or famous person, usually for political reasons.
fact: «Terminate with extreme prejudice» is US spy slang that means assassinate.
fact: The word tells the reader that a killing was planned and aimed at someone important.
fact: Assassinate is a serious word about violence, so it is used in history lessons and news about famous leaders who were killed.
exercise: «The plotters planned to assassinate the king.» What does assassinate mean? | To paint a famous picture | To give a grand speech at a party | *To murder an important person, usually for political reasons | To lose a game on purpose
exercise: Which form of the verb shows that it already happened: assassinate, assassinates, assassinated or assassinating? | *assassinated | assassinates | assassinate | assassinating
exercise: «Terminate with extreme prejudice» is spy slang. What does it mean? | *Assassinate, murder an important or chosen person on purpose | Leave the room quietly | Argue loudly about a rule | Finish a school project early
test: Why does the word assassinate tell the reader that the killing was planned? | Because it means a car accident | *Because it is aimed at someone important and done on purpose | Because it is always a happy story | Because it is written in a comic book
test: Which school subject would most likely use the word assassinate? | Music, about rhythm | Maths, about shapes | Art, to name colours | *History, about famous leaders who were killed
exam: Read «The leader was assassinated in his palace.» What kind of person was killed? | A stranger passing by in the street | *An important person, such as a leader | A pet rabbit | A character in a cartoon
